AB  - As cloud computing technology matures and becomes more widespread, internet-based businesses and applications of artificial intelligence become increasingly intricate. Enterprises are now more sensitive to factors such as data sensitivity, compliance requirements, and personalized needs. The surge in demand for extensive and diversified computing power is propelling the growth of the cloud hosting industry. Consequently, the expectations from cloud hosting now encompass requirements for comprehensive capabilities, security, and open compatibility. Enabling computing power, ensuring compatibility with the full-stack ecosystem, and optimizing security systems have emerged as inevitable trends in the evolution of cloud hosting services. This paper delves into the technical architecture and operational framework of full-stack cloud hosting, leveraging a range of cloud-native technologies including containers, micro-services, and DevOps. Additionally, a holistic approach to security system design is proposed to address the security challenges inherent in full-stack cloud hosting. Through tiered deployment and multi-level isolation, this approach aims to enhance the efficiency of cloud hosting business operations while providing robust security protection for cloud resources from various angles.
