AB  - This paper presents the design of a service system with modular architecture that automates and optimizes critical stages of the recruitment process in the software domain. The proposed solution is based on a hybrid approach structured in two complementary stages. The first stage performs the automatic classification of candidate CVs into eight of the most in-demand IT roles (Data Scientist, Machine Learning Engineer, DevOps Engineer, Backend/Frontend Developer, QA Engineer, Project Manager and Cloud Architect) using the XGBoost algorithm and leveraging the contribution of each element from semantic features (education, soft skills, programming languages, certifications, foreign languages and professional experience) in the final matching score. The second stage introduces a novel interpretability and manual adjustment mechanism, enabling recruiters to redefine the relative importance of different skill categories from the semantic features defined above, so that scores generated by the model align more closely with the company’s specific requirements at a given time. The service system, currently under development, operates in a containerized environment and is orchestrated through Kubernetes technology to ensure scalability and component isolation.
ER  - 

