AB  - The growing reliance of contemporary applications on machine learning (ML) has revolved CI/CD pipelines into MLOps, or DevOps with the force of AI. As ML models are incorporated into production pipelines, scalability, reliability, and compliance become increasingly important. Adding ML into CI/CD introduces new problems, such as complex data governance, expensive retraining, probabilistic validation, and persistent surveillance to detect drift and ensure fairness. This survey thoroughly examines emerging models, research, and tools throughout the ML development pipeline—from data pipelines to model construction, deployment, tracking, and security. Along with demonstrating exciting developments in automation, containerization, and DevSecOps practice, our analysis also identifies ongoing scalability, explainability, and interoperability limitations. By projecting contributions onto life-cycle phases and closing typical gaps, we introduce a systematic taxonomy and comparative overview that highlights the research landscape. Finally, this overview provides both a snapshot of existing solutions and a glimpse of an agenda for advancing engineering of adaptive, explainable, and reliable MLOps pipelines for the research and practitioner community.
ER  - 

