AB  - The optimization of cloud resources stands essential for DevOps workflows, yet companies face difficulties when maintaining reliability at affordable costs. The research explores AWS environments to analyze the implementation of Reserved Instances together with Spot Instances when addressing cost-reliability trade-offs. A combination of Reserved Instances with Spot Instances which provides stable production workload coverage and fault-tolerant capabilities produces substantial cost savings without unacceptable MTTR increases according to real-world experimental analysis. Technical solutions for this implementation consist of load balancers that provide failover capabilities and checkpointing methods that preserve state information while EC2 Auto Scaling automates instance recovery processes. The analysis demonstrates that excessive Reserved Instance procurement results in underutilized resources and Spot Instance testing interruptions create longer recovery durations. Hybrid models solve deployment problems while they enhance high deployment speeds through reduced lead time variations. The research investigates machine learning technologies and multi cloud solutions as potential strategies for optimizing dynamic resource utilization in the future. The research discovers practices that support operational leaders in adjusting their cloud resource utilization per organizational requirements.
ER  - 

